cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "The L 198-93 candidate was first posted by Branden Murray (doi:10.5281/zenodo.23230562); cite that record for the candidate. If you use this vetting, its ephemeris or this code, please cite it as below."
title: "L 198-93 (TIC 264151965): independent vetting of the 4.82-day transit candidate pre-registered by Murray (2026)"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Paliwal
    given-names: Advait
    email: advaitpaliwal@gmail.com
version: "1.1"
date-released: "2026-11-11"
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/advaitpaliwal/TIC264151965"
url: "https://github.com/advaitpaliwal/TIC264151965"
abstract: >-
  Independent vetting of the 4.8158 d transit candidate on the M dwarf
  L 198-93 (TIC 264151965) at 21.2 pc, posted first by Murray (2026,
  Zenodo, doi:10.5281/zenodo.23230562) with a pre-registered test in TESS
  Sectors 113 and 114. TESS Sectors 38, 65 and 99 to 102 give period
  4.8157979 +/- 0.0000050 d (1.0 sigma from Murray's), mid-transit BJD_TDB
  2459336.1785 +/- 0.0015, depth 1255 +/- 66 ppm, duration 1.16 h, radius
  1.16 (+0.05/-0.04) Earth radii. Pixel fits in all six sectors place the
  dip on the target. False-positive probability 0.079 without companion
  limits and 0.020 +/- 0.009 with MOLUSC Gaia companion limits, no
  neighbours removed, and no high-resolution imaging, so a planet
  candidate, not a validated planet.
keywords:
  - exoplanet
  - transit
  - TESS
  - planet candidate
  - M dwarf
  - L 198-93
  - TIC 264151965
